# Source material the site is built FROM but never serves: design-tool
# exports, reference PDFs, scans. Kept on disk, never committed.
#
# This ignore is the only thing keeping it off the live site. GitHub Pages
# serves every file in the published branch, and `.nojekyll` switches off the
# filtering that would otherwise skip underscore-prefixed paths — so a
# `git add -f _source/` would publish a 2.7 MB PDF at a guessable URL.
_source/

# Source workbook for the Income Tax Ledger. Same reasoning as _source/: the
# site is built from it but never serves it, and at the repo root it would
# publish at a guessable URL. Nothing links to it.
Tax_Bracket_Ledger_Docs.xls

# Working folders that live beside the site but are not part of it. Same
# reasoning as _source/ above: GitHub Pages serves every file in the published
# branch, so the only thing keeping these off the live site is not committing
# them.
#
#   data analytics/          a Python teaching workspace — a 252 MB .venv, a
#                            32 MB .pptx, a 24 MB case data file, licensed case
#                            PDFs, and the IRS workbooks. The one file the site
#                            needs is the built dashboard, copied into
#                            dashboard/irs-soi/ and committed from there.
#   sample tax return …/     a 39-page practice return PDF carrying SSN-shaped
#                            values, names and an address.
data analytics/
sample tax return for testing/
